Rules:
- Fill in every field. Where the request is ambiguous or silent, make the most reasonable
  assumption for a typical web application of this kind and state it as one of `open_questions` -
  do not leave the spec incomplete or refuse to answer.
- Every feature must have an `id` (short, e.g. "F-01"), a `name`, a `description`, a `priority`
  ("must", "should" or "could") and at least one concrete, testable `acceptance` criterion.
- `roles` lists every distinct type of user; every `pages[].roles` entry must be one of them.
- `entities` are the core data models (e.g. "User", "Order"); give each entity's fields their
  name, a simple type ("string", "int", "boolean", "datetime", "decimal", ...) and whether it is
  required, plus any `relations` to other entities in plain text (e.g. "belongs to User").
- `security_level` is "standard" unless the request describes handling of sensitive data (health,
  payments beyond a standard checkout, government IDs), in which case use "high".
- `stack` defaults to "golden-v1" (Next.js + FastAPI + PostgreSQL) unless the request explicitly
  asks for something else.
- Use `open_questions` only for things that materially affect scope or architecture and that you
  had to guess at - not for minor wording.

